---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { SITE } from '../consts';

/**
 * Photo is picked up automatically — drop a file at `src/assets/profile.jpg`
 * (or .png/.webp) and it appears. Absent, the text runs full width.
 */
const matches = import.meta.glob<{ default: ImageMetadata }>(
  '../assets/profile.{jpg,jpeg,png,webp}',
  { eager: true }
);
const photo = Object.values(matches)[0]?.default;
---

<div class:list={['about', photo && 'about--with-photo']}>
  {
    photo && (
      <div class="about__photo">
        <Image src={photo} alt={SITE.name} widths={[240, 480]} loading="lazy" />
      </div>
    )
  }

  <div class="about__text">
    <p>
      I've spent 14 years building games in Unity — mobile, multiplayer, VR and cross-platform.
      That's covered live titles past 100 million downloads, a real-money platform where security
      was the first constraint, a VR collaboration product, and a multiplayer strategy game I led
      from an empty repository through to live operations.
    </p>

    <p>
      What I keep coming back to is architecture — not as a diagram exercise, but as the thing that
      decides whether a team can still move quickly in month eighteen. Most of my work is building
      systems that stay extendable under a real production schedule: clear ownership, testable
      seams, and no clever code that only one person understands.
    </p>

    <p>
      I use AI tooling daily — Claude Code and GitHub Copilot — across planning, architecture
      review, debugging and test generation. It's earned its place most in the planning phase,
      catching problems in existing code before they reach production.
    </p>

    <p>
      The personal projects on this site are those same ideas with the source open. You can read the
      code rather than take my word for it.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .about {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .about--with-photo {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 14rem) minmax(0, 1fr);
    align-items: start;
    gap: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .about__photo :global(img) {
    width: 100%;
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  }

  .about__text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  @media (max-width: 46rem) {
    .about--with-photo {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .about__photo {
      max-width: 11rem;
    }
  }
</style>
